
          -- Zeus Bulletin Board System - Version 1.1 History --

o Fixed minor error in FSC-0039 packet headers in ZMP and ZGate.  They
  weren't setting the CW-Validation field which wasn't present in the older
  FSC document I had!

o ZAPP now works over serial links!

o Added %L code for programs spawned from ZMailer.  Expands to the line
  number.

o ZMailer will now accept EMSI strings with fido illegal hex escapes in as
  generated by DBridge.

o Fixed problems with ZMP updating its config.

o ZGate now processes news batches properly!

o ZMP's AreaFix %RESCAN command now takes an optional number argument
  to specify the maximum amount of messages that should be rescanned.

     %RESCAN ALL 100
     %RESCAN AMIGA 200

o Zeus' input translation tables now work again!

o New Zeus Rexx Commands:

     SUBTIME <ON|OFF>

     ON  - Subtract minutes from users Minutes Left counter (as normal)
     OFF - Freeze users Minutes Left counter
     
     * Asynchronous function - needs line number

     ZAPP '"<Program> <Args>"' [WAIT]

     Spawns a ZAPP program from Zeus:Bin/Zapp/ with the given args.  This
     command will return immediately unless the WAIT flag is given, in
     which case, ZAPP will not return until the program has completed.

     Examples:

        ZAPP '"PlayPCM 'Line' DH3:PCM/asteroid.pcm"'
        ZAPP '"MountNFS 'Line' Files:"'
        ZAPP '"SendMsg 'Line' \"This is a test!\""' 'WAIT'

     Returns:
     
        -1 if program couldn't be started, return code from program if in
        WAIT mode, else zero.

     * Asynchronous function - needs line number

o zeuszapp.device was crashing on ZCMD_FREESCREEN.

o You can now set ZMP's Inbound and Outbound directories in ZMP.cfg:

     INBOUND    Mail:In/
     OUTBOUND   Mail:Out/

o Wrote Zeus:Bin/MakeBatch for creating news batches from single articles.

o Wrote Zeus:Bin/xBatch for extracting UU/Base64 Encoded binaries from news
  batch files.

o Wrote ZappPrefs for setting all the options in zapp.device via a nice
  GUI.  This will be part of the user package and isn't actually needed
  by Zeus.

o Changed some of the zapp.device prefs arguments.  Run ZappPrefs to
  reconfigure and ignore the error requester telling you it can't parse
  the prefs file.

o DETECTZAPP now takes an argument which specifies the amount of tenths of
  a second it should wait before aborting the ZAPP handshake.  Defaults to
  five (half a second).

